method Erase bbox pngalpha
    How this device clears its page, where clearing it is not painting
    it white. A device without one is painted white by erasepage, which
    fills the page with the ground through the ordinary marking methods
    (data/paint.ps). These two cannot be cleared that way: the extent
    tracker would take the full-page fill into the box it is
    accumulating, and the alpha device clears to transparent, which is
    not a colour any fill can name.
    The device that paints nothing carries none, and that is the right
    answer rather than an omission: it holds nothing a page reset
